CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ called: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ deduced: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Fixed: decltype(invoke()) in a static data member's initializer, where
invoke calls a member template with a deduced return type, was not int
while the class was instantiated: element<2>'s deferred definition was
converted on demand, but the call kept the placeholder type, so invoke's
return type was not deduced (the "template 'element' not found" was a
later probe of element<N>(1) as a functional cast).
